{"request": "optimize my LinkedIn headline and about section", "expect": "linkedin-best-practices-2026", "why": "profile optimization, distinct from the LinkedIn content specialist subagent"}

// --- Hiring artifacts: candidate brief vs. general presentation/brand skills ---
{"request": "build a candidate brief for this frontend engineer, here's the assessment and CV", "expect": "candidate-brief", "why": "competency radar + CV artifact, not a general slide deck"}
{"request": "turn this hiring assessment into a scorecard with a competency radar chart", "expect": "candidate-brief", "why": "radar-chart hiring artifact should not fall to dataviz or riverside-presentation"}
// --- Podcast transcription: episode links vs. generic web/data skills ---
{"request": "can you summarise this https://open.spotify.com/episode/5ej5YQIPjZkvd19IRUJIdY", "expect": "podcast-transcript", "why": "Spotify episode link needs the RSS-feed + local-transcription path, not a plain WebFetch of the DRM-locked page"}
{"request": "transcribe this podcast episode and give me the key takeaways", "expect": "podcast-transcript", "why": "transcribe-an-episode is this skill, not content-agent or a data query"}
{"request": "what have Creator Marketing and Growth Channels spent this month on the invoices board", "expect": "invoice-board-spend-pulse", "why": "Board-sourced totals for the two teams this skill actually covers. Guards against mesh-expenditure-report, which reports Mesh card spend rather than monday board invoices."}
{"request": "send Nir the spend pulse for the invoice board", "expect": "invoice-board-spend-pulse", "why": "Names the pulse and its recipient. Guards against invoice-inbox-to-monday, which files invoice emails rather than reporting board totals."}
{"request": "who on the team has not uploaded their receipts to Mesh", "expect": "mesh-expenditure-report", "why": "Receipt chasing is Mesh-side. Guards the reverse direction against invoice-board-spend-pulse, which only reports monday board invoice totals by team and does no receipt chasing."}
// --- DE organic report vs the whole-site organic dashboard ---
{"request": "can you pull the German site's organic search numbers for last month vs the month before, per URL", "expect": "seo-de-report", "why": "single-locale per-URL organic funnel report with a custom/date-driven range, not the 7-page whole-site organic-dashboard"}
{"request": "give me the full organic analytics dashboard with rankings and search console, not just the DE numbers", "expect": "organic-dashboard", "why": "guards the sibling: whole-site multi-source retrospective should not fall to the DE-only per-URL report"}
{"request": "before this draft goes out, verify the product claims in it are actually true", "expect": "demo-reply-fact-check", "why": "claim verification on prospect-facing copy is the fact-check gate, not the drafting skill"}
{"request": "is async recording really Business-plan only or am I making that up", "expect": "demo-reply-fact-check", "why": "plan-gating verification with a tier claim, the exact failure mode the ledger exists for"}
{"request": "find duplicate tickets across the MOPs and website boards", "expect": "ticket-hygiene", "why": "duplicates are the sweep's Pass A; mops-backlog-review audits stale parked work, not redundant work"}
{"request": "this website task is sitting on the marketing ops board, should it move", "expect": "ticket-hygiene", "why": "Pass B board routing; the near-miss is monday-agent doing a raw move with no rules"}
{"request": "which slack requests from this week never became tickets", "expect": "ticket-hygiene", "why": "mops-standup surfaces intake gaps but hands filing here, since this skill holds the permalink ledger"}
{"request": "which open website tickets are missing a figma or a brief", "expect": "ticket-hygiene", "why": "Pass C readiness sweep over existing tickets; pm-story only gates at creation time"}
{"request": "scan the mops channels and open tickets for anything untracked", "expect": "ticket-hygiene", "why": "INTAKE mode; must not land on mops-standup, which reports the day rather than filing"}
{"request": "audit how well this skill is written and score its authoring quality", "expect": "skill-audit", "why": "authoring-quality rubric, distinct from skill-eval routing and health-check staleness"}
{"request": "half our skills are badly written, rewrite the worst few and only keep what measurably helps", "expect": "skill-optimizer", "why": "fix-and-verify loop across the library, not a single-skill audit score"}
{"request": "loop over the whole skill library: edit whatever scores lowest, re-measure, and undo anything that did not improve", "expect": "skill-optimizer", "why": "applies and judges edits; skill-eval only proposes description patches"}
{"request": "manage my routines, I want to change one of my scheduled triggers", "expect": "raz-ops", "why": "Raz's personal routine/task orchestration layer, not a department-wide skill"}
{"request": "remember that I don't want Slack pings on weekends", "expect": "raz-ops", "why": "standing personal preference with no live system, routed to raz-ops which saves it to Claude Memory"}
{"request": "check my open tasks and move my Tuesday invoice pulse to Friday", "expect": "raz-ops", "why": "personal current-state-plus-change request; must not land on chief-of-staff (Nir's leader-level brief) or mops-standup (Hanan/Jonathan's shared standup)"}
{"request": "create a task to review the new landing page copy", "expect": "pm-story", "why": "sibling check - net-new monday task creation still belongs to pm-story even though raz-ops now exists; raz-ops delegates creation to pm-story rather than owning it"}
{"request": "what do I need to add to this week's report", "expect": "raz-ops", "why": "on-demand recall of the report-notes ledger - must not land on invoice-board-spend-pulse or nir-weekly-report, which are different people's different reports"}
{"request": "here's the brief for the new editor launch video, let's kick it off", "expect": "video-project-intake", "why": "Raz handing over a creative video brief is the Creative Ops front door, not generic monday task creation"}
{"request": "stress-test this video brief before it goes to the team", "expect": "video-project-intake", "why": "Gate 0 brief grading lives in intake; must not fall through to content-agent or marketing-brain"}
{"request": "start a new video project on the creative board", "expect": "video-project-intake", "why": "project creation on 18426224074 duplicates a template group; pm-story and monday-agent must not touch this board directly"}
{"request": "here are a few links, figure out what they are and what I should do with each", "expect": "link-triage", "why": "the core link-triage trigger - classify pasted links then decide per link; must not fall through to marketing-brain as generic cross-system work"}
{"request": "read this article and pull anything useful for us", "expect": "link-triage", "why": "single-link mine-for-insights path belongs to link-triage, not content-agent (which produces artifacts) or riverside-intel (which is the file-to destination, not the reader)"}
{"request": "open a ticket for this - Ann needs the homepage banner live tomorrow, copy is BREAKING NEWS: Meet AI Twin, linking to riverside.com/ai-twin", "expect": "pm-story", "why": "a Trendemon on-site message reaching the board - ticketing intent plus a placement and copy. Near-misses are page-cro and webflow-link-checker, which would analyse the page instead of filing the request; the board choice itself (MOPs, not Website Dev) is enforced inside pm-story Step 6, not here"}
{"request": "please create a Marketing Ops ticket for the request", "expect": "pm-story", "why": "the word is ticket, not task - pm-story's description carried no ticket vocabulary until 2026-09-02, so ticket-hygiene outranked it and a single-ticket creation would have triggered a board-wide hygiene sweep"}
// --- Content pipeline: three skills, three verbs. Register choice is the risk. ---
{"request": "draft a slack message asking the US team who Vince should talk to", "expect": "nik-voice", "why": "writing in Nir's voice routes to the router first, not straight to slack-agent, which owns delivery rather than wording"}
{"request": "this reads like ChatGPT wrote it, fix it", "expect": "de-ai", "why": "slop removal on an existing draft, not a re-voicing job for nik-voice"}
{"request": "make it more human, add some personality", "expect": "de-ai", "why": "guards the retired content-humanizer trigger: de-ai absorbed it, so this must not go looking for a second humanizer"}
{"request": "is this LinkedIn post actually any good before I post it", "expect": "critique", "why": "a verdict on finished writing, not a rewrite; critique scores and never edits"}
{"request": "write up the funnel numbers for me, keep it short", "expect": "ste", "why": "internal functional output for Nir skips the outward-facing pipeline entirely"}
// --- weekly organic conversion report vs the monthly organic dashboard ---
{"request": "how did organic do last week", "expect": "weekly-seo-report", "why": "a single completed 7-day window is the weekly conversion report, not the monthly retrospective"}
{"request": "run the weekly seo report", "expect": "weekly-seo-report", "why": "the report's own name, exactly as the SEO team asks for it"}
{"request": "weekly organic numbers, visits signups and subs with the week over week move per landing page", "expect": "weekly-seo-report", "why": "per-URL funnel at weekly grain is the weekly report's core table"}
{"request": "clicks and impressions in the SEO sheet have not moved in days, is google still sending us anything", "expect": "gsc-freshness-check", "why": "a freshness question about the feed, not a request to build the weekly SEO report or the organic dashboard"}
{"request": "refresh the SEO dashboard with our Ahrefs ranking movement and AI overview share", "expect": "organic-dashboard", "why": "guards the sibling: rank tracking and AI-overview share are deliberately excluded from the weekly report and belong to the monthly dashboard"}
{"request": "refresh the organic dashboard for last month with the content cohorts", "expect": "organic-dashboard", "why": "guards the sibling: monthly grain plus content cohorts, which the weekly does not pull"}
{"request": "the weekly report for Nir on what MOPs and website dev shipped", "expect": "nir-weekly-report", "why": "guards the reverse direction against /weekly-seo-report; this one is monday task state for Nir, not search performance"}
// --- Value proposition canvas vs its neighbours. The risk is theft from page-cro, marketing-psychology, win-loss, content-agent. ---
{"request": "build a customer profile for agencies - what are their jobs, pains and gains", "expect": "value-proposition-canvas", "why": "the canvas vocabulary itself; must not fall to marketing-psychology's six-line JTBD stub or to content-agent, which writes rather than profiles"}
{"request": "do we actually have fit between what we sell and what B2B content teams need", "expect": "value-proposition-canvas", "why": "a fit question about the offer, not a page audit (page-cro) and not a closed-lost coding job (win-loss-pricing-analyzer)"}
{"request": "write a test card for the hypothesis that producers care more about guest setup than editing", "expect": "value-proposition-canvas", "why": "test card and learning card are this skill's artifacts; measurement-agent reads results out, it does not design the hypothesis"}
{"request": "what should we even be saying to solopreneurs, who is this really for", "expect": "value-proposition-canvas", "why": "positioning before copy: content-agent and nik-voice write once the Value Map exists"}
{"request": "draft customer discovery interview questions for next week's power user sessions", "expect": "value-proposition-canvas", "why": "customer discovery interviews, not curious-intern, which interviews colleagues about our own systems"}
{"request": "audit the agency page for conversion barriers and tell me what to change above the fold", "expect": "page-cro", "why": "incumbent guard: a page audit stays with page-cro even though the new canvas skill mentions segments and fit"}
{"request": "why are we losing enterprise deals on price this quarter", "expect": "win-loss-pricing-analyzer", "why": "incumbent guard: closed-lost coding with revenue attached stays with win-loss; the canvas skill only consumes its pain section"}
{"request": "what mental models explain why people hesitate on the pricing page", "expect": "marketing-psychology", "why": "incumbent guard: biases and mental models, not a customer profile or a value map"}

