// --- Impeccable (vendored design skill) vs the Riverside brand/UX skills and page-cro. The risk runs both ways: a craft pass on a built surface must land on impeccable, a brand fact or conversion question must not. ---
{"request": "polish this dashboard html before it goes to Nir, the type hierarchy and spacing feel off and the cards are nested in cards", "expect": "impeccable", "why": "a craft pass on a built UI surface; riverside-ux-patterns is the near-miss on 'spacing' and 'hierarchy', but it is the standard impeccable loads, not the pass itself"}
{"request": "this hero design is bland and timid, make it bolder and more delightful, keep the copy as is", "expect": "impeccable", "why": "amplifying a timid design is an impeccable command (bolder); page-cro and page-build are the near-misses on 'hero' but this is craft, not conversion barriers or a ticketed build"}
